After several weeks, the landlord came to Clark's apartment to evict him. #id:5b
He didn't answer the door. #id:5c
No one lived there. #id:5d
The landlord called the police and they opened the door. #id:5e
What they found was... #id:5f
...disturbing. #id:60
They found out Clark's body in bed. #id:61
He looked extremely weak. #id:62
He was hugged to what it used to be his GameStation 69 #id:63
"What a loser", the landlord said. #id:64
Before leaving the apartment, the landlord saw something written on the wall using what appeared to be blood. It said\: #id:65
"I NEEDED MORE" #id:66
javi: Whoa, that was a bit strong. #id:67
javi: Hello there! My name's Javi. The developer of what you just experienced. #id:68
javi: Well, sorry if I traumatized you too much. #id:69
javi: Writing has always been a great passion for me and so is gaming so I thought of combining both in this game. #id:6a
javi: Just to clarify, no dog or granny was harmed during the development of this game. #id:6b
javi: Just as a reminder, the game is open source and licensed under the GPL 3 #id:6c
javi: You can check itch io page of the game, or its source code below #id:6d
label link_options #id:6e
- Check itch page #id:6f
	do Global.open_url("https://google.com")
	jump link_options
- Check source code #id:70
	do Global.open_url("https://github.com/javiermoralesdev/INeedMore")
	jump link_options
- Return to main menu #id:71
	javi: Once again, thank you por playing my game. #id:72
	do Global.change_scene("main_menu")